## How to Build Each Item

When tackling any unchecked item:
1. Read the relevant reference repo first (@references/...)
2. Check rules/rules.md — does this touch trading logic?
3. Write the script to agent/
4. Test it: python3 agent/[script].py
5. If it passes, check it off in this file
6. Commit: git add . && git commit -m "complete: [item name]"

## Auto-Commit Rule

After completing any checked item:
```
git add .
git commit -m "complete: [what you just built]"
git push
```

This keeps the repo always up to date. No manual commits needed.
